From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 01:02:17 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] winspool, gdi32, localspl: Save Print Output As -- the Print to PDF printer asks where its PDF goes, Print to file asks for a .prn (9814)

Windows asks where a printed file goes with the Save dialog "Save Print
Output As": a PDF named after the document for Microsoft Print to PDF,
Printer Files (*.prn) for Print to file. Our Print to PDF printer is the
CUPS queue on cups-pdf (sg-print-setup): every PDF went to Documents under
a name of cups-pdf's making without asking, and Print to file asked in a
bare "Output File Name" box.

- winspool: StartDocDlg asks with the Save dialog: for a printer whose CUPS
  queue is on cups-pdf (device URI cups-pdf:), when the document has no
  output of its own (none, or the printer's port, as programs pass their
  DEVNAMES port to CreateDC), PDF Document (*.pdf) named after the document
  in Documents; for Print to file, Printer Files (*.prn). Cancel is
  ERROR_CANCELLED.
- gdi32: StartDoc whose Save Print Output As was cancelled prints nothing
  and fails with ERROR_CANCELLED, as on Windows.
- localspl: the PDF printer's job written to the chosen file is PostScript
  (cups-pdf's PPD); it is made a PDF in place with Ghostscript (pdfwrite,
  -dSAFER), as cups-pdf would have. A file the program names itself is not
  asked for and is made a PDF too. Linux programs keep cups-pdf.

Gate test/pdfprint-gate.sh.

